communication_activities:
• In 2020 WB6 CIF has, jointly with EC, established WB6 - EU Business Platform with aim to facilitate dialogue between EU policy makers and WB6 business community on how to leverage up European accession perspectives to create more opportunities for trade, investment and other forms of business cooperation between the two sides. The Platform also seeks to identify problems that businesses face either in cross-border activity or in the application of EU regulation and to influence the formulation or implementation of concrete policy or legislation, or the decision-making processes of the EU institutions policies and to suggest concrete solutions. 
In the last 3 years 4 meetings of the Business Platform have been conducted and 2 additional, tailor-made meetings with local SMEs and EU decision makers on following topics: 

• Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/159 of 31 January 2019 imposing definitive safeguard measures against imports of certain steel products; 
• EU Green Deal
• Energy Taxation Directive and EU Single-Use Plastic Directive;
• Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism (CBAM);

• 2026: Entry/Exit System (EES) - WB6 CIF submitted a joint appeal (Title: Urgent Invitation to a High-Level Coordination Meeting on Western Balkan Border Disruptions (EES)) to the European Commission regarding the position of professional drivers in international road transport, with particular emphasis on the application of the 90/180-day rule and border procedures. Through this appeal, the WB6 CIF clearly warns about the consequences of policies that directly affect companies, increase business costs, and threaten the stability of trade flows between the European Union and the Western Balkans. (https://www.wb6cif.eu/9777/)

