Create Abundance Foundation CLG (Ireland) engages with EU institutions primarily in relation to the following EU policy frameworks and initiatives:

– The EU Charter of Fundamental Rights, in particular Articles 10 (Freedom of thought, conscience and religion), 21 (Non-discrimination), and 23 (Equality between women and men);

– EU policies and strategies on gender equality and women’s empowerment, including the EU Gender Equality Strategy;

– EU initiatives related to mental health, emotional well-being and psychosocial resilience, including actions under the EU Health Union and related public health frameworks;

– EU education and lifelong learning policies, including initiatives promoting inclusive education, social cohesion and community resilience;

– EU policies addressing social inclusion, civil society participation and fundamental rights.

The organisation’s activities may involve participation in public consultations, policy dialogues, expert roundtables, civil society forums, conferences and awareness-raising events organised or supported by EU institutions. These interactions aim to contribute perspectives related to emotional resilience, women’s empowerment, freedom of belief and community well-being.

