eu_legislative_proposals:
In 2024-2025, four projects financed by CERIC-ERIC, under the “Expression of Interests” call, have started: 
-	ESBY (Electron microscopy for Structural BiologY at CERIC-ERIC) will allow the installation of a new  cryo-confocal microscope Stellaris 5 by Leica (ref. L. Vaccari); 
-	STEAM (multiScale TErAhertz iMaging), provided a new offline instrument, now fully operational, for the TeraFERMI beamline (ref. A. Perucchi);
-	FAITH (Flexible Apparatus for Imaging and TomograpHy) aims to upgrade one of the microCT offline instrument in the Tomolab (ref. D. Dreossi);
-	Bat-ERIC is dedicated to the Battery Lab and will provide users with a complete pipeline of instruments and know-how for the study of energy materials, from sample preparation to sample measurements (ref. J. Plaisier).	
All these projects are allowing new instruments to be added to the Italian Partner Facility offer in CERIC-ERIC. 

Among the European projects, it is worth mentioning ERA_SHUTTLE (Accelerating ERA by Sharing Unique Talents for Healthy Life and Environment) : the Horizon Europe WIDERA scheme allows researchers to learn from world-level research centers and implement the acquired knowledge at their home institutions once back. Within ERA_SHUTTLE, Elettra will work with CERIC-ERIC to host 3 experienced researchers from the Universities of Gdansk, Split and Malta in our offline laboratories TOMOLAB, SISSI-BIO-OFF and NanoInnovation (ref. C. Blasetti). 

Elettra’s researchers are involved in several COST Actions, fostering networking and training for your researchers. The SNOOPY project will bring together a network of experts and young innovators from diverse disciplines (chemistry, biology, biochemistry, materials science, nanotechnology, medicine, physics) to overcome existing barriers to predict and implement bioactive peptides' ability to self-assemble into functional nanostructures, including those at the interface with membranes, potentially forming pores and channels (ref. B. Rossi). The ENRICH COST Action aims to strengthen connections among different radiation detection physics sub-communities. ENRICH will be promoting collaboration among existing communities to achieve significant advancements on X-ray and gamma rays photon detections, photons sources, data analysis and data acquisition, beyond the current state of the art (ref. A. Gianoncelli).

goals:
Het HNP heeft de volgende doelstellingen gedefinieerd:

(1) Het verbeteren van de contacten van de Nederlandse provincies met de Europese instellingen, de Nederlandse Permanente Vertegenwoordiging (PV) bij de EU en andere regionale bureaus in Brussel;

(2) Synergie tot stand brengen tussen de provincies om te komen tot een efficiënte vertegenwoordiging van de gezamenlijke belangen;

(3) Het verstrekken van voldoende en tijdige informatie over het Europees beleid en de HNP-activiteiten;

(4) Het bijdragen tot een betere kennis en bewustwording in de Nederlandse provincies van het Europees integratieproces;

(5) Het verlenen van de faciliteiten voor het adequaat ontvangen van bezoekers.

BlueLink is a foundation, registered in public interest in Bulgaria to uphold civil society, democracy, shared European values and environmental sustainability. BlueLink strives to its purpose by supporting internet networking, public interest journalism, policy advocacy and research.

BlueLink's main fields of activity are in:
-maintaining the BlueLink Civic Action Network - a networking, coordination and information exchange hub at www.bluelink.net; 
-supporting civil society participation, access to information and justice, and stakeholder engagement through strategic use of internet and other activities;
-operating a virtual newsroom to publish Evromegdan (in Bulgarian) and BlueLink Stories (in English, for Central and Eastern Europe) as e-magazines for ethical journalism in public interest; and
- fostering research and analysis of internet freedom, technological and social change, civil society, democracy and sustainable development, and shaping policies that foster them.

