goals:
IUSTO is a private University aggregated to the Faculty of Education of the Pontifical Salesian University, working in the field of academic and specialist education with:
i) advanced training courses and graduate and post-graduate programs in pedagogy, psychology, communication and human sciences;
ii) education programs for workers, experts and professionals;
iii) study, research and documentation;
iv) education and training events, based on the needs of the community and of society.
Currently, IUSTO offers three Bachelor Degree programs and four Master’s Degree programs. Moreover, a number of Master's and University Courses are proposed each year.
In addition, IUSTO is accredited by the Piedmont Regional Office as Education Agency in the fields of superior and continuing education and of vocational activities.
Since 2013 IUSTO joined the academic world circuit of the Salesian University Institutes, a network with 95 centres worldwide.

