communication_activities:
Festival is the strongest component of EXIT platform but it is not the only one. It is followed by strong and numerous social activities, campaigns and projects. There are more than 100 projects of EXIT Foundation, and some of the most important ones are (just to name a few):
2015-2016 – Team of Exit foundation was successfully leading candidacies of the city of Novi Sad  for European Cultural Capital 2021 and European Youth Capital 2019;
2013 – Youth Heroes award – giving media attention to the prominent young people in society in opposition to bad influences for youth that are promoted through reality shows, commercial press, etc;
2012 – Youth Fair – Exit is organizing regional youth tourism fair in Novi Sad;
2006-2009 – campaign for EU visa liberalization for citizens of Western Balkans (The EU Commissioner for Enlargement, Mr. Olli Rehn spoke at the discussion stage at EXIT Festival);
2004-2008 – Campaign against human trafficking conducted together with MTV Foundation (global campaign;
2002 – Serbia are you ready for the future? – campaign promoting EU values and transition in Serbia after Milosevic’s rule;
Following are the information regarding latest campaigns and projects:
1. Creative History Balkans Tour – Regional Coorporation Council / EU 2018-2019 - project that aims to develop and promote the tour based on four historical fortresses in four Balkans’ countries: Petrovaradin Fortress in Novi Sad, Serbia; Citadela Fortress Old City of Budva, Montenegro; Kastel Fortress in Banja Luka, Bosnia and Herzegovina; and Skadar Fortress in Rozefa, Albania. (www.creativehistorybalkans.com)
2. Cultural-Contemporary Tourism Route – IPA CBC Hungary – Serbia 2018-2020 Using cultural heritage and contemporary art as tools, the projects aims to establish new cross-border linkage and to develop a new tourist route that will help in improving tourism offer and model of managing regional offer through creation of a new tourism products based on the cultural and touristic potentials.
3. HEMI - The Hub for the Exchange of Music Innovation (HEMI) is an umbrella of music networks and communities of the CSEE working to strengthen and expand the horizontal value chain and cooperative model among the joining organizations operating in the wider Music Industry and in the Live Music sector. Supported by the Creative Europe programme.
4. MOST - The Complex Strategy to develop Balkan World Music Scene - aims to improve the world music market of the Balkans by a complex strategy including audience development, professional training, export support mobility of artists and professionals, event management, platform development, policy suggestions and pilot projects. The project focuses on world music, the musical segment that enhances communication between different cultures. Supported by the Creative Europe programme.
5. EXIT TreeZone - Thanks to numerous nature lovers, over 400 volunteers, Fruška Gora has become richer  for 13,000 seedlings of Sessile oak on the 23. November 2019. This large action was executed by EXIT Foundation and EU Delegation as part of the Natura2000 Project. “Give back to nature – Join, plant a tree!”, a joint initiative of EU delegation and EXIT Foundation was started at last year’s edition of EXIT Festival. This is just a first in the series of large ecological actions by EXIT, that with this afforestation launches its big ecological platform symbolically entitled “Green Я:Evolution“! The aim of this unique platform is to mobilise public and start afforestation in the country, Region and world, which in Serbia alone has been planned planting of over a million trees.
6. Green EXIT - together with EU Delegation to Serbia and our festival foodland partners and suppliers working on recycling and less plastic.
7. EMERGENCY EXIT – communication and awareness-raising campaign combining art, technology and environmental storytelling to raise public awareness of climate change and ecological responsibility.

goals:
The mission of the Platform is to improve oral health and enhance cost-effective prevention of oral diseases in Europe.
Our goal is to create a common European approach towards improved oral health education, promotion, and access to care in Europe.
Our approach is to:
- Encourage oral health and the prevention of oral diseases as a fundamental to good general health;
- Enhance the EU’s oral health policy, including incorporating oral health in to relevant policies;
- Secure EU action on oral health;
- Address oral health inequalities and challenges, especially among vulnerable populations like children and adolescents, the elderly, and those with special needs.

