As a trade association, LuxCMA is actively engaged in shaping regulatory policy and fostering sound market practices across the capital markets ecosystem.
Our work is closely aligned with the evolving European regulatory landscape and centres around key legislative initiatives and policy priorities. 
These currently include, but are not limited to:

- Capital Markets Union (CMU) and Savings and Investment Union (SIU), including the Retail Investment Strategy (RIS);
- Sustainable Finance Package (incl. Taxonomy Regulation, SFDR, EU GBS, CSRD, CSDDD)
- Digital Finance Package (incl. Pilot Regime, MiCA and DORA)
- Implementation and revision of the Prospectus Regulation;
- Listing Directive
- Listing Act Initiative
- Implementation of the Securitisation Regulation (STS framework);
- Implementation of the Securities Financing Transactions Regulation (SFTR);
- Implementation and review of MiFID II / MiFIR, notably regarding the consolidated tape and post-trade transparency for non-equity instruments;
- Implementation of CSDR, in particular regarding settlement discipline measures;
- Review of the Market Abuse Directive and Regulation (MAD II / MAR);
- Review of EMIR, in particular the introduction of the Small Financial Counterparty (SFC) regime;
- Regulatory developments related to wholesale Central Bank Digital Currency (CBDC);
- Broader geopolitical and macroeconomic trends with market impact.

Through its working groups and advocacy efforts, LuxCMA provides a platform for expert-driven dialogue and delivers constructive input to policymakers, regulators, and other stakeholders, with the aim of supporting a competitive, resilient, and forward-looking capital markets environment.

