communication_activities:
Throughout 2025, the Spanish Aggregates Federation (Federación de Áridos – FDA) has continued to represent and promote the collective interests of the Spanish aggregates industry before national and European institutions. Through its direct activities and its active participation in Aggregates Europe (formerly UEPG), the Federation has contributed to the development, implementation and promotion of European policies affecting the aggregates sector and the wider construction materials value chain.
A major milestone during the year was the organisation of the VII National and International Aggregates Congress, held in Córdoba in October 2025. The Congress brought together representatives from the European Parliament, the European Commission, the Council of the European Union, Spanish public authorities, industry leaders, academics and other stakeholders. The event provided a unique platform to discuss the strategic role of aggregates in the green and digital transitions, the implementation of European industrial and environmental policies, the security of supply of essential raw materials, and the future competitiveness of the sector.
The Congress also served as a forum for dialogue between policymakers and industry representatives, enabling constructive exchanges on regulatory developments, sustainability objectives, permitting procedures, innovation, biodiversity, circular economy and industrial decarbonisation.
Throughout 2025, FDA has maintained a continuous dialogue with national administrations and European institutions, both directly and through Aggregates Europe, with the objective of contributing to better regulation, more effective implementation of existing legislation and the development of policies that support sustainable mineral resource management.
In particular, FDA has consistently advocated for the recognition of aggregates as an essential and strategic raw material underpinning Europe’s housing, transport, energy and industrial infrastructure objectives. The Federation has highlighted the indispensable contribution of aggregates to the successful implementation of European policies relating to the energy transition, climate neutrality, territorial cohesion, affordable housing and strategic autonomy.
Particular attention has been devoted to legislative and policy initiatives related to:
• The implementation of the Critical Raw Materials Act (CRMA);
• Circular economy and resource efficiency policies;
• Nature restoration and biodiversity legislation;
• Industrial decarbonisation measures;
• Environmental permitting and administrative simplification;
• Public procurement frameworks;
• Sustainable construction policies;
• Climate neutrality and emissions reduction objectives;
• Competitiveness and regulatory burden reduction initiatives.
As part of its commitment to sustainability and transparency, FDA has actively contributed to several sectoral initiatives developed at European level through Aggregates Europe. These include the promotion and dissemination of the Aggregates Declaration of Environmental Performance, aimed at improving environmental transparency and reporting across the sector, as well as the development of the Aggregates Neutrality initiative, which seeks to strengthen the sector’s contribution to climate, biodiversity and circular economy objectives.
The Federation has also continued its collaboration with the Network for Nature Restoration and other environmental stakeholders to promote best practices in quarry restoration, biodiversity enhancement and post-extraction land use. 
FDA’s advocacy and institutional activities are guided by a number of core principles:
• Sustainable supply of aggregates and mineral resources;
• Environmental stewardship and biodiversity enhancement
• Industrial competitiveness and strategic autonomy;
• Regulatory stability and legal certainty;
• Occupational health and safety;
• Innovation, skills development and talent attraction.

