The AQUA ! association, launched on the 15th of December 2023 in France, is dedicated to the study, protection and promotion of water heritage. With a European dimension, it is open to citizens, associations, local and public stakeholders, experts and scientists. 

AQUA ! promotes a civic, democratic and societal vision of water as a common good at the crossroads of a number of specific expectations.

It focuses in particular on "hybrid" hydrosystems, notably hydraulic structures and all their appendages (ponds, swamps, water bodies, reservoirs, lakes, canals, diversion bays, managed rivers, etc.), their conception, management, landscapes, uses and the socio-economic life that surrounds them, through various actions:
•	advocacy / publications;
•	training / coaching;
•	collaborative projects ;
•	mapping and data analysis ;
•	toolkits on mediation and consultation;
•	communication and territorial animation

Eurodad (the European Network on Debt and Development) is a network of 58 civil society organisations (CSOs) from 28 European countries, which works for transformative yet specific changes to global and European policies, institutions, rules and structures to ensure a democratically controlled, environmentally sustainable financial and economic system that works to eradicate poverty and ensure human rights for all.

Our focus is on strengthening the power of European CSOs, working as part of a global movement to push governments and powerful institutions to adopt transformative changes to the global economic and financial system. 

Eurodad's Strategic Plan sets ambitious goals to help achieve: tax justice to stem the loss of resources in developing countries; 
ending debt crises that hinder economic progress; effective aid that will transform lives; 
publicly-backed private finance and investment agreements that accelerate development results; 
