eu_legislative_proposals:
Climate Parliament engages with Members of the European Parliament and officials of EU institutions on issues relating to renewable energy deployment, climate finance, sustainable development and international climate cooperation, particularly in Africa and Small Island Developing States. Activities have focused on policies and initiatives including:

The European Green Deal (COM(2019) 640 final);
The European Climate Law (Regulation (EU) 2021/1119);
The EU Global Gateway strategy and related initiatives supporting sustainable infrastructure and renewable energy investment in partner countries;
The Neighbourhood, Development and International Cooperation Instrument – Global Europe (Regulation (EU) 2021/947);
EU policies and programmes relating to climate finance, energy transition, sustainable transport and international climate partnerships.

Climate Parliament facilitates dialogue between parliamentarians, policymakers, technical experts and development partners on the implementation of these policies, with a particular focus on accelerating renewable energy deployment, strengthening parliamentary engagement in climate governance and mobilising investment for low-carbon development.

communication_activities:
Climate Parliament organises and participates in a range of communication and stakeholder engagement activities related to the EU policies and initiatives listed above. These activities include parliamentary roundtables, policy dialogues, conferences, study visits, publications, briefings and stakeholder meetings involving parliamentarians, EU policymakers, development partners and technical experts.

Recent examples include:

Meetings and exchanges with Members of the European Parliament and EU officials on renewable energy deployment, climate finance and EU-Africa climate cooperation;
Organisation of virtual and in-person parliamentary roundtables bringing together legislators from Africa, Europe and Small Island Developing States to discuss climate policy, renewable energy and sustainable development;
Publication of policy briefings, event summaries and other communications materials on Climate Parliament's website and communication channels;
Participation in international climate and energy events that facilitate dialogue between parliamentarians and EU stakeholders on climate action and clean energy investment.

