KHIMOD’s activities are primarily related to European Union policies and initiatives supporting industrial decarbonisation, clean technologies, renewable and low-carbon hydrogen, carbon dioxide utilisation and sustainable fuels.

The main relevant EU policy and legislative frameworks include:

Regulation (EU) 2024/1735 on establishing a framework of measures for strengthening Europe’s net-zero technology manufacturing ecosystem (Net-Zero Industry Act);
European Union policies and initiatives related to renewable and low-carbon hydrogen, including the European Hydrogen Bank;
European Union policies supporting the development and deployment of renewable fuels of non-biological origin (RFNBOs), including renewable hydrogen and e-fuels;
European Union policies and funding initiatives supporting industrial decarbonisation, carbon capture and utilisation (CCU), and innovative low-carbon technologies.

At this stage, KHIMOD’s activities mainly consist of preparing and submitting projects for recognition, labelling and participation in relevant European initiatives and platforms.

