communication_activities:
- contributed to the 2020, 2021,2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026 Rule of Law Reports of the EU Commission;
- sent various letters and correspondence to Eu Commission and EU Council, urging for the adoption of the Rule of Law Conditionality Regulation;
- contributed to the targeted consultation in the context of the preparation of the strategy on the effective application of the Charter of Fundamental Rights in the EU;
- urged in various letters (and in an in-person meeting with Commissioner Reynders, in Brussels, in January 2020) for the importance of initiating and moving forward in article 7 TEU proceedings against Poland and Hungary, regarding Rule of Law backsliding;
- sent letters to President Von der Leyen and Commissioners Reynders and Jourova regarding the various CVM reports regarding Bulgaria and Romania;
- sent numerous letters and statements to EU Commission regarding the situation and ongoing reforms in candidate countries where MEDEL has members (Serbia, Montenegro, Moldova and Turkey), denouncing attacks against the independence of the Judiciary;
- organised conferences destined to influence EU actors, such as the "Conferences in view of the EU Parliament elections" (https://medelnet.eu/index.php/activities/medel-conferences/495-cycle-of-conferences-democracy-and-rule-of-law) or the "Rule of Law in Europe" conference, where Commissioner Didier Reynders participated (https://medelnet.eu/index.php/activities/medel-conferences/785-rule-of-law-in-europe-conference-lisbon-2021); 
- organised "conferences on the eve of the June 2024 election for European Parliament" , inviting as speakers Members of EP  (https://medelnet.eu/medel-conferences-on-the-eve-of-the-june-2024-election-for-european-parliament-florence-5-april-2024-rome-12-april-2024-paris-31-may-2024/):  Florence 5 April 2024 (Democracy and the Rule of law in Europe: critical issues and open challenges on the eve of the European elections -https://medelnet.eu/medel-conferences-on-the-eve-of-the-june-2024-election-for-european-parliament-florence-5-april-2024-rome-12-april-2024-paris-31-may-2024/); Rome 12 April 2024 (Immigration in Europe and Fundamental Rights. Which perspectives for the next European Legislature? https://medelnet.eu/medel-conference-on-the-eve-of-the-june-2024-election-for-european-parliament-immigration-in-europe-and-fundamental-rights-which-perspectives-for-the-next-european-legislature-rome/); Paris 31 May 2024 ( Le rôle des magistrats dans la construction démocratique – une perspective européenne, https://medelnet.eu/medel-conference-on-the-eve-of-the-june-2024-election-for-european-parliament-paris-31-may-2024/)
-in 2024 took part in the project promoting Rule of Law Report; 
-in December 2024 was present at the meeting with Polish MoJ organised at the Permanent Representation of Poland, in Brussels, to present the priorities for the justice sector in view of the upcoming Presidency; - on 10 March 2025 published  with other NGOs in Le Monde  the collective article "Civil society in peril: Europe must respond to the freeze on US aid";-in April 2025- in an in-person meeting with Commissioner McGrath in Brussels-  presented its activity vis-à-vis RoL backsliding in Europe; on 4 April 2025  joined the collective NGOs statement calling on the EU to defend the ICC; -on 22-23  April participated in the International Conference “The role of civil society in the protection of the rule of law”, organised in Warsaw by the Polish MOJ, under the Polish Presidency of the EU Council;-on 3 June 2025 organized a conference at the Palace of Europe Strasbourg focused on current challenges to democracy, justice and RoL where the EU FRA Director Sirpa Rautio took the floor while Comm. Mc Grath intervened with a message https://medelnet.eu/medels-40th-anniversary-conference-3-june-2025-strasbourg/

eu_legislative_proposals:
CRTA's EU-level advocacy and awareness-raising activities primarily relate to EU policies and processes concerning Serbia's democratic development and EU accession, electoral integrity, rule of law, media freedom and pluralism, countering disinformation and foreign information manipulation and interference (FIMI), civic participation and the environment for civil society.
Key EU documents and processes concerning Serbia:
- European Commission annual Serbia Reports and the annual EU Enlargement Package, including the Serbia Reports for 2018-2025; 
- EU Enlargement Policy and Enlargement Strategy; 
- Serbia's EU accession negotiations, particularly issues related to the Fundamentals cluster, democracy, rule of law, fundamental rights, functioning of democratic institutions, electoral reform and media freedom; 
- EU Rule of Law Mechanism and annual Rule of Law Reports, including their application to enlargement countries; 
- Growth Plan for the Western Balkans, Reform and Growth Facility and Serbia's Reform Agenda; 
- EU enlargement reforms and preparations for a larger Union ("pre-enlargement policy reviews and reforms"); 
- European Parliament resolutions concerning democracy, elections, rule of law, media freedom and political developments in Serbia, including the European Parliament resolutions on the situation in Serbia issued in 2024, 2025, 2026, as well as the European Parliament report following the ad hoc AFET mission to Serbia in 2026. 
Relevant horizontal EU policies and initiatives:
- European Democracy Shield; 
- European Democracy Action Plan; 
- EU Defence of Democracy package; 
- EU policies and initiatives on electoral integrity, free and fair elections and democratic participation; 
- Digital Services Act, particularly provisions and guidance concerning systemic risks to civic discourse, electoral processes and disinformation; 
- Code of Conduct on Disinformation under the Digital Services Act; 
- European Media Freedom Act; 
- EU policies and measures addressing disinformation and Foreign Information Manipulation and Interference (FIMI); 
- EU policies on media freedom, media pluralism and the safety and protection of journalists; 
- EU policies concerning rule of law, fundamental rights, civic space and the enabling environment for civil society; 
