The Macau European Chamber of Commerce unites European businesses in Macau in joint efforts to influence trade rule and regulation improvements in the interest of European businesses.

As a business Chamber, MECC is mostly devoted to follow the trade and economic relationships of Macau SAR with EU and European business as operating worldwide.

Thus, the focus of our attention would be:
i) trade agreements between Macau, EU and mainland China; 
ii) any legislation adopted within EU that could affect, impair or improve international trade, in particular with Greater China (including mainland China, HK, Macau and Taiwan);
iii) any international agreement to which EU becomes a party that could affect, impair or improve international trade, in particular with Greater China;
iv) any regular meetings or summits, in particular with a focus on trade or investment, with Macau, Hong Kong and mainland China;
v) any legislation adopted within EU or any international agreement enacted by EU that could affect, impair or improve investment from Europe in greater china and vice-versa.

