It is EurEau’s mission to promote the common interests of its members to the EU institutions and to keep its members informed of relevant developments in the European arena.

In practice this results in the following main activities:

 • To promote the common interests of the European water service sector to the EU institutions and stakeholders;
 • To enable its members to adequately deal with opportunities and threats arising from EU policy and its national implementation;
 • To support members’ networking.

In line with this, EurEau aims for a provision of reliable and high quality water supply and waste water services which:

 • Protect public health;
 • Fully respect the natural environment;
 • Support economic development;
 • Remain socially acceptable.

As per Article 3 of the SME Safety Statute:

- The main objective of the association, constituted as a non-profit international association in accordance with the Chapter III of the law of 27 June 1921 on non-profit associations, non-profit international associations and foundations, is to safeguard the interests of European SMEs in the safety sector in the international regulatory and policy domain (SMEs are referred to hereby as defined in the EU recommendation 2003/361: http://eur-lex.europa.eu/LexUriServ/LexUriServ.do?uri=OJ:L:2003:124:0036:0041:EN:PDF.) 

In order to reach this overall goal, the association is committed:
- to represent the interests and stances of the organization's Members on specific problems vis-à-vis the European and international standardization bodies;
- to represent the interests of the members vis-à-vis the European and international institutions;
- to provide information to the Members on the development of standards and legislation in the safety sector.

