In order to fulfil this aim, the DSTF serves primarily the following purposes: 
•	to foster the implementation of “Sturgeon 2020”-Strategy, as published by the DSTF in 2013, 
•	to provide a platform for exchange of information and experience on sturgeon conservation in the Danube Basin; 
•	to facilitate cooperation between the key sturgeon conservation stakeholder groups as science, policy level and non-governmental organisations and to foster synergies with other organizations involved in Danube sturgeon conservation; 
•	to raise awareness of decision makers and the public as well as to build c (...)

The fund is organised exclusively for charitable, scientific and educational purposes: development, monitoring and evaluation of prevention programmes to improve public health worldwide.
Specifically it:
o	undertakes and supports scientific research;
o	provides technical assistance to governments and other organisations and training programmes;
o	pilots international grant programmes;
o	collaborates financially and technically with local and international foundations and organisations working to improve global health in the following areas, not limited to: tuberculosis, HIV/AIDS, asthma, childhood tuberculosis, tobacco control, road safety, collection and analysis of public health statistics; sponsoring scientific publications, conferences and workshops.

