communication_activities:
The European Food Forum hosts regular multi-stakeholder debates, policy dialogues, expert exchanges and other activities on a wide range of issues related to the European agri-food system and its economic, social and environmental context. These activities aim to facilitate transparency, mutual understanding and an evidence-based exchange of perspectives among policymakers and stakeholders.

Topics addressed through EFF activities include, inter alia:

- the future, competitiveness and resilience of the European agri-food sector;
- food security and the resilience of food supply chains;
- sustainable food systems and the transition towards more sustainable production and consumption;
- agriculture and the future of the Common Agricultural Policy;
- food safety, including developments affecting plant protection and agricultural production;
- nutrition, public health, healthy and sustainable diets and consumer information;
- food labelling, environmental information and consumer empowerment;
- food processing, innovation and the evolving role of technology in food production;
- biotechnology, research and innovation in the agri-food sector;
- food loss and food waste prevention;
- packaging, circularity and the environmental footprint of food systems;
- sustainable sourcing, deforestation-free supply chains, traceability and due diligence;
- climate change, biodiversity and the environmental sustainability of agriculture and food production;
- animal welfare and sustainable livestock production;
- protein diversification and the role of different protein sources in European food systems;
- skills, education and generational renewal in the agri-food sector;
- international trade and the global competitiveness of the European agri-food sector;
- access to food, affordability and the social dimension of the transition towards sustainable food systems; and
the contribution of the agri-food sector to the UN Sustainable Development Goals.

