-	Accountancy Europe (ex Fédération des Experts-comptables Européens) qui suit l’agenda et l'actualité de la Commission Européenne;
-	La Fédération Internationale des Experts comptables et commissaires aux comptes Francophones (FIDEF), la Fédération Panafricaine des Experts-Comptables (PAFA) et la Confédération des Experts-comptables d’Asie et du Pacifique (CAPA) ;
-	Mais aussi d’autres organisations internationales tel que l’Integrated Reporting Council (IIRC).

goals:
Geopa is the European association officially recognised by the European Commission as the European social partner representing 22 national employer associations in the agricultural sector.
Geopa's objectives are:
i. To develop effective strategic policies and initiatives to promote the agricultural sector as a safe, fair and prosperous working environment;
ii. To represent the national employer associations for the agricultural sector in all European public platforms such as the European social dialogue, the European Platform Tackling Undeclared Work and the European Agency for Safety and Health at Work;
iii. To support the implementation of EU legislation and initiatives such as the Pact for Skills with a view to guarantee the prosperity and sustainability of the sector in Europe.

ANIA, the Italian insurance association, was established in 1944. It is the representative body for mutual, cooperative and joint-stock insurance and reinsurance companies in Italy. It covers 85% of the Italian insurance market. The main objectives of ANIA are:
- to negotiate collective agreements with trade unions and to promote initiatives aimed at encouraging professional training;
- to carry out studies in order to solve problems dealing with techical, economic, financial and legislative matters and to perform information, advisory and assistance activities for members.

