Annual public art interventions and festivals engaging over 100,000 citizens, revitalising public spaces in Zagreb and beyond through artistic and participatory urban regeneration (e.g. Project Ilica: Q’ART);

Educational programs and workshops linking creativity, ecology and social cohesion – with direct relevance to the Green Deal and social innovation agendas;

Visual campaigns and community publications focused on inclusion, diversity, and rethinking public space as a shared cultural and ecological resource;

