goals:
The Federation was established in July 2016 through the merger of the Fédération française des sociétés d'assurances (FFSA) and the Groupement des entreprises mutuelles d'assurance (GEMA).

It brings together all insurance and reinsurance companies operating in France, comprising 247 companies that account for more than 99% of the overall insurance market.

Our main missions are to:

- safeguard the full range of economic and social interests relating to insurance activities;
- represent the insurance industry before national and international public authorities, institutions, administrative bodies and market authorities;
- provide a forum for discussion and analysis of financial, technical and legal issues;
- provide key statistical data on the insurance industry;
- inform the public and the media;
- promote risk prevention and resilience initiatives;
- promote the role of insurance in academia and education and training.

