- PR Army team has distributed 15 media pitches on the Disarm Russia topic among 1,200 media contacts in the
USA, United Kingdom, France, Germany, Switzerland, Austria, Sweden, Belgium, Spain and Japan. This resulted in
publications in Tier1 media;
- PR Army also covered European campaigns to stop trade with Russia and support pro-Ukrainian activists' demos in
Europe;
- a press conference in Paris on forcible deportations of Ukrainians held in Nov 2022 resulted in 72 media publications (online, print, TV, radio, podcast) with an approx reach of 2.1 mln people in 19 countries; we’ve facilitated over 200
publications on the topic as of now;
- 30 individuals involved in the deportations were sanctioned in the EU and US based on our research and data;
- held a webinar The Forcible Transfer and Deportation of Ukrainian Children by Russia: Search for
Solutions together with Georgetown University Collaborative on Global Children's Issues;
- convened 2 offline events in Kyiv, Ukraine having gov.authorities as speakers on the issue of forcible passportization on the TOT of Ukraine and on detention camps in Russia and the TOT of Ukraine;
- we made an investigation into the participation of the Russian Orthodox in the deportation of
Ukrainians.

