Our participation in the Conference on Countering Fake Election Observation, Disinformation, and Hybrid Threats, organized by the European Platform for Democratic Elections (EPDE), aligns with our focus on EU initiatives aimed at safeguarding electoral integrity and democratic resilience. In this context, our interest relates primarily to:

European Democracy Action Plan (EDAP) – especially aspects addressing disinformation and election integrity;

Digital Services Act (DSA) – particularly its provisions on transparency and accountability of platforms in countering disinformation;

EU Code of Practice on Disinformation;

Strategic Compass for Security and Defence, in the context of hybrid threats;

EU Action Plan against Disinformation (2018) and its ongoing implementation.

Our engagement aims to support policy measures that strengthen democratic institutions, transparency in elections, and counter disinformation and foreign interference.

goals:
Improve the treatment and quality of life of patients with Congenital Heart Disease (CHD) by information on appropriate medical, surgical and psychosocial therapies, in particular regarding long-term outcomes and unifying statistical methodology;
Integrate paediatric and adult cardiac treatment, and in particular to install and provide a smooth “transition” for adolescents from paediatric to adult;
Promote and sustain scientific and medical research in all fields of CHD;
Represent the interests of CHD patients in national and European health policy;
Raise public awareness of CHD and to instill in the public an understanding of the concerns of people with CHD;
improve the safety of treatments for children and adults;
Advocate European regulations for off-label use and special treatment needs (i.e., paediatric).

