We are interested in staying informed and contributing to relevant policy developments concerning food distribution, sustainability, and logistics. In this regard, we follow recent and ongoing initiatives such as:
– Proposal for a Regulation on packaging and packaging waste (COM/2022/677 final);
– Proposal for a Regulation on establishing a framework for ensuring a secure and sustainable supply of critical raw materials (COM/2023/160 final);
– Proposal for a Regulation on establishing a framework of measures for strengthening Europe’s net-zero technology manufacturing ecosystem (Net-Zero Industry Act);
– Revision of EU legislation on food information to consumers (announced in the Farm to Fork Strategy and expected soon);
– European Commission public consultations and roadmaps in the area of food contact materials and environmental labeling.
As a food distribution company expanding into renewable energy and electric logistics, we are committed to aligning with EU sustainability and food safety standards, and we remain open to contributing to future consultations or stakeholder dialogues.

