MMC’s engagement focuses on EU policies and legislative initiatives that impact the battery value chain, critical raw materials, and strategic trade relations. Key areas of interest include:

The EU Battery Regulation (Regulation (EU) 2023/1542), particularly provisions related to battery sustainability, responsible sourcing, and carbon footprint reporting;

The Critical Raw Materials Act (CRMA), supporting efforts to strengthen EU access to strategic battery materials such as high-purity manganese;

The EU Green Deal and related initiatives advancing electrification, clean energy, and circular economy principles;

Trade policy instruments, such as the Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism (CBAM) and bilateral trade agreements, including trade relations between the EU and the United States under the TTC (Trade and Technology Council).

MMC seeks to contribute to a resilient and transparent supply chain for battery-grade manganese while supporting policy frameworks that incentivize sustainable, non-Chinese mineral supply.

