The GIE objectives comprise mainly but are not necessarily limited to those listed:

1.Contributing to a safe and reliable European transmission system suitable for meeting present and future transportation needs;
2.Supporting the European Union on its path to deliver the EU Green Deal’s objectives;
3.Enhancing decarbonisation of all regions and sectors, including the hard-to-abate ones;
4.Supporting the development of the hydrogen economy with the existing gas infrastructure and via the development of innovative projects;
5.Promoting market solutions;
6.Contributing to the setting of a stable public policy framework;
7.Voicing the opinion of the its members in Europe according to the previous points.

