European Union external human rights and democracy policies concerning Türkiye, including the European Union–Türkiye human rights dialogue and related political and institutional processes;

European Union financial and civil society support policies and programmes relevant to human rights defenders, equality, youth participation and civil society organisations in Türkiye.

goals:
The EU Dog & Cat Alliance was created in 2014. Our members are organisations from across the EU and the UK, including veterinary organisations, organisations which are involved in the rescue/rehoming of dogs and cats and organisations which are working to protect dog and/or cat welfare. The Alliance’s main focus is on improving EU legislation in relation to dogs and cats. We aim to: 
- Lobby the European Union to introduce and improve EU legislation in relation to dogs and cats, and engage in other EU activities; 
- Engage with other key EU stakeholders and collaborate wherever possible to improve the welfare of dogs and cats in the EU; 
- Provide a constructive platform for the sharing of information on dog and cat welfare issues between our members; 
- Gather robust evidence on the dog and cat issues we work on and produce reports and briefings to support our position. 
The EU Dog & Cat Alliance works on issues which are of priority to dogs and cats in the EU.

eu_forums_and_platforms:
The EU Dog & Cat Alliance was established in October 2014. The Alliance primarily focuses on: 
Dog and cat breeding and trade; 
Movements of dogs and cats across Member State borders; 
Online advertising of dogs and cats for sale.

goals:
NIO designs, develops, manufactures and distributes premium smart electric vehicles and drives next-generation innovation in autonomous driving, digital technologies, electric powertrains and batteries. NIO sets itself apart through its continuous technological breakthroughs and innovations, such as its industry-leading battery replacement technologies, Battery as a Service (BaaS), as well as its proprietary technologies for autonomous driving and Autonomous Driving as a Service (ADaaS).

The role of the NIO Brussels Office is to:
- Anticipate, monitor and analyse relevant EU policy developments;
- Inform relevant departments and support subsequent amendments to company products or practices;
- Provide input, where necessary and appropriate, to EU decision-makers through policy statements, responses to public consultations or impact assessments;
- Represent the company and its interests in relevant EU forums.

eu_legislative_proposals:
Our organization, 100% LIFE, is a charitable patient-led NGO that works to improve access to quality healthcare and essential medicines, including HIV/AIDS and other socially significant diseases, with over 15 years of experience in Ukraine.

We are interested in activities related to the harmonization of Ukrainian pharmaceutical legislation and practices with EU standards, as part of broader efforts to facilitate the integration of Ukrainian pharmaceutical manufacturers into the European market.

Specifically, our interest representation activities concern:

EU pharmaceutical legislation, including regulatory alignment with:
Directive 2001/83/EC on the Community code relating to medicinal products for human use;
Regulation (EU) 2017/745 on medical devices;
Regulation (EU) 2019/6 on veterinary medicinal products (where relevant to general GMP compliance and regulatory practice);

Emergency preparedness legislation, including alignment with the objectives of the Health Emergency Preparedness and Response Authority (HERA) and ensuring supply chain resilience across Europe;

EU Enlargement and Eastern Partnership policy, especially in the context of pre-accession support for legal and market harmonization in the health and pharmaceutical sectors.

We seek to engage in policy discussions that support:
Mutual recognition of GMP certification between Ukraine and EU Member States;
Enabling the production of quality-assured generic medicines in Ukraine for EU supply;
Removing regulatory and legal barriers to the inclusion of Ukrainian pharmaceutical products in the European market.

L’organisation souhaite assister à des événements, consultations et espaces de réflexion liés aux politiques de l’Union européenne dans les domaines de la justice raciale, de la justice climatique, de l’égalité de genre et des relations euro-africaines.

Dans ce cadre, African Futures Lab suit de près les initiatives suivantes, qui orientent ses travaux et analyses :

Plan d’action de l’Union européenne contre le racisme 2020-2025 (Communication de la Commission, COM/2020/565 final) ;

Plan d’action pour l’égalité de genre III (JOIN/2020/17 final) ;

Stratégie globale de l’Union européenne avec l’Afrique (JOIN/2020/4 final) ;

Résolution du Parlement européen sur les droits fondamentaux des personnes d’ascendance africaine en Europe (2018/2899(RSP)) ;

Loi européenne sur le climat (Proposition de règlement COM/2020/80 final).

