goals:
The Bulgarian Ladies’ Forum is a nonprofit organization, established in the end of December 2009. it gathers 130 women in senior management positions in large companies or who are successfully developing their own business. The organization is a platform for sharing experiences and ideas, as well as supporting future women leaders through special initiatives. 
The main goals of the Forum are:
•	to create better opportunities  for professional realization and comprehensive improvement of women engaged in business;
•	to work for the affirmation of women, as leaders in business and a factor in the construction of civil society, being a guarantor of democracy;
•	to ensure cooperation with other non-governmental and governmental bodies and organizations and to support gender equality and other charitable and philanthropic causes.
• to organize discussions, trainings, mentoring and educational initiatives and events in order to empower women to start, grow and sustain successful businesses.

eu_forums_and_platforms:
Partnership with European Women on Boards

In 2022 We became a partner of European Women on Boards, the largest European association promoting gender equality in senior management and boards across Europe, whose aim is to ensure a diversity of experience, skills, views and expertise in line with the needs of Boards of Directors and promoting best management practices, combining efficiency and ethics to enable management teams to fulfill increasing duties and responsibilities in an increasingly complex decision-making environment and creating governing bodies, leading by example, evaluating any available talent in the company;
Our representatives actively participate in the working group at the European level, which will prepare a strategy and develop specific guidelines for the transposition of the EU directive on gender balance among directors of listed companies and related measures.

