goals:
TPN is a non-governmental network firmly rooted in the worlds of business and politics, but also open to administrators and academics on both sides of the Atlantic. Its objectives are as follows:
First, to facilitate informal constructive dialogue at a strategic level between the worlds of business and politics on both sides of the Atlantic with the involvement of Government and academic representatives;
Second, to help this partnership adjust to new challenges and opportunities; to identify common interests and to reduce the scope for misunderstandings between business and governments on either side, and to promote and assist the convergence of EU/US Government policies;
Third, to act as a communications mechanism for ideas on policy issues.  Wherever possible, TPN works with established organisations and institutions, avoiding duplication and enhancing specific objectives.
TPN does not itself take positions on specific issues nor does it represent specific interests.

The European Committee for Homeopathy represents medical doctors, pharmacists, veterinarians and agronomists specialized in homeopathy, organized in 40 associations in 28 European countries. It is aimed at

- promoting the scientific development of homeopathy;
- ensuring high standards in the education, training and practice of homeopathy by registered health professionals;
- harmonising professional standards in homeopathic practice across Europe;
- providing high-quality homeopathic care in a safe medical context;
- integrating high-quality homeopathy into European health systems.

XReg Consulting is a regulatory consultancy firm that specialises in crypto-assets. We assist our clients in designing their regulatory and compliance strategy. We are committed to steering crypto-asset public policy in a way that supports innovation and fosters a sound, stable, and globally cooperative approach. In addition to raising our organisation's profile in Brussels, our goal is to support our clients' efforts in the following ways:
- trying to shape EU policy to ensure that new requirements are practical and consider intended and unintended consequences;
- supporting their participation in consultation processes;
- engaging with relevant institutions and policymakers; and
- participating at EU and global events to support the growth and innovation of the crypto-asset market (e.g. organising events and webinars concerning the EU's Digital Finance Package, participating in panels as speakers and moderators, etc.).

Our organization enables stakeholders to make better decisions by applying the latest science on chemicals in food contact materials and on the environmental impacts of food packaging. This includes:

- Raise awareness for hazardous chemicals in all types of food contact materials and articles as well as for the environmental impacts of all types of food contact materials and articles, by communicating the latest science;

- Connect different stakeholders that can make decisions leading to the removal of hazardous chemicals in all types of food contact materials and articles, and reducing the environmental impacts of all types of food contact materials and articles;

- Conduct research about chemicals in food contact materials and articles, and their impacts on human and environmental health.

