One of IGLYO's strategic goals is to advance on the access and recognition of children and young people's rights to achieve full equality without discrimination based on sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression and sex characteristics. We work to strengthen LGBTQI children and youth rights, ensure equality and inclusion, and represent the intersectional needs of LGBTQI children and young people. 

We achieve this within international, European, national and local policy and legal mechanisms on the following topics: 
- Bias-motivated violence and hate speech;
- Children and youth autonomy;
- Education;
- Family;
- Freedom of assembly, association and expression;
- Health;
- Legal gender recognition;
- Sports.

As a result all of our activities and work that fall under the scope of the Transparency Register is conducted to advance such human rights and equality to LGBTQI children and youth.

goals:
ATAG promotes a united global vision for aviation and provides a collaborative environment to foster the exchange of ideas, joint approaches to common issues and a united voice to ensure governments, industry and civil society can work together to progress the sustainable development of air transport. ATAG:
- develops studies to provide reliable data on aviation's contribution to job creation, trade, tourism, community lifelines and humanitarian disaster response;
- establishes working groups to address solutions to key challenges;
- minimises long-term environmental and climate impacts of aviation and air transport connectivity;
- advocates for coordinated action on strategic issues; mobilises joint statements; 
- provides expert contributions to governmental and UN processes.
- develops an array of communications resources about aviation's sustainability activities;
- organises educational and information-sharing sessions at events and other fora for a variety of audiences.

AFCDP, the largest DPO organisation in France, aims at defending the interest of Data Protection Officers.
To that end, it seeks to : 
- promote the position in organisation, by demonstrating its usefulness;
- propose a network allowing exchanges of thoughts, ideas and good practices, in France and in Europe;
- design and examine useful tools, methods and practices; 
- defending the position by monitoring the evolution of its legal framework;
- be a point of contact for the French data protection authority.

ARDITI is the Regional Agency for Research, Technological Development and Innovation (located in Madeira island, Portugal). It is a Private non-profit public utility association. The aim of ARDITI is to promote and support Research, Technological Development and Innovation (RTDi) within Autonomous Region of Madeira, namely by:
• Supporting the regional government of Madeira in the definition and implementation of science and technology policies, namely on the regional smart specialization strategy (RIS3-RAM);
• Participating and funding RTDi projects, providing scholarships for researchers (including PhD and Postdoctoral grants). ARDITI also integrates researchers participating in specific projects;
• Promoting and disseminating RTDi results and their adoption in the business, service and industrial sectors.

