communication_activities:
PEPPPA conducts communication activities aimed at promoting awareness, understanding, and uptake of the Pan-European Personal Pension Product (PEPP) in line with Regulation (EU) 2019/1238 and broader EU goals such as the Capital Markets Union and long-term savings policy.

These activities include:

Organizing and co-hosting webinars, workshops, and policy briefings with EU stakeholders, including EIOPA and DG FISMA;

Publishing policy position papers, implementation guidance, and comparative studies on PEPP rules and best practices;

Running awareness campaigns targeted at self-employed workers, mobile citizens, and cross-border professionals to explain the benefits of PEPP;

Producing newsletters and reports summarizing regulatory developments and industry responses;

Participating in EU public consultations, such as those on PEPP tax treatment, financial literacy, and digital pension tools.

