goals:
Estonian Association of Newsmedia Enterprises is an non-profit organisation working in the common interests of newspapers, journals, online-portals, TV and radio channels. 
Association aims at defending the common interests and rights of newsmedia, proceeding from internationally recognized principles of democratic journalism.

To fulfil its goals Association:
•	represents newsmedia by influencing processes relating to newsmedia (lobby in parliament, distribution, printing, advertising, ownership);
•	develops co-operation with media organisations in Estonia and abroad;
•	offers members a chance to exchange ideas and compare notes in a professional environment; 
•	in conjunction with Press Council, upholds good journalistic practice and fights against violations of the freedom of the press;
•	promotes access to public information as a right of every citizen;
•	organises training courses for newsmedia managers and editors, arranges contests for journalists;
•	collects and publishes media

