The company does not act on behalf of third parties in interest representation.

For transparency purposes, we indicate the EU legal instruments and policy frameworks that may be relevant to our operations, compliance monitoring and event-related communications (e.g. participant information, registration and online presence). These include in particular:
– General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) – Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (data protection in event registrations, mailing lists, and communications);
– Digital Services Act (DSA) – Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 (online communications and platform-related obligations);
– European Accessibility Act (EAA) – Directive (EU) 2019/882 (accessibility considerations and participant information, where relevant);
– EU Climate Law – Regulation (EU) 2021/1119 and sustainability-related EU initiatives applicable to events (e.g. waste prevention and reduction measures, including the Single-Use Plastics Directive (EU) 2019/904).

Any interaction with EU-level initiatives is limited to participation in publicly available stakeholder events/webinars, factual information exchanges and compliance-related monitoring.

