is_member_of:
El declarante es Eventísimo SLU, que opera bajo el nombre comercial BEON Worldwide (https://beonworldwide.com
). Eventísimo SLU es una empresa privada de responsabilidad limitada y no cuenta con miembros ni entidades afiliadas en el sentido previsto en el apartado 12 del Registro de Transparencia.

Eventísimo SLU no representa intereses de miembros, dado que no es una asociación, federación, red ni organización basada en afiliación. En consecuencia, no existen personas físicas o jurídicas que deban declararse como miembros.

Asimismo, Sun&Blue Congress no constituye una entidad jurídica con estructura de membresía. Se trata de un congreso y foro profesional organizado por Eventísimo SLU, sin miembros ni entidades afiliadas.

Las entidades que figuran en la página web de Sun&Blue Congress (https://sunandbluecongress.com
), bajo la sección “Partners”, corresponden exclusivamente a instituciones y organizaciones que han contribuido con contenido, conocimiento o participación en la edición 2025 del Congreso. Estas entidades no son miembros ni afiliadas, ni implican relación estructural, vínculo de capital, control común, coordinación en actividades cubiertas por el Registro o patrocinio en el sentido previsto en las directrices del apartado 12.

goals:
TÜSİAD is the non-governmental representative organisation of the Turkish private sector (industries, finance and services) at the national level  |  over 55% of the economic added-value (80% of exports) 85% of corporate tax revenues. It is the leading business organisation in Turkey.
TÜSİAD is a member of BUSINESSEUROPE, Global Business Coalition, BIAC (Business and Industry Advisory Council of the OECD), BusinessMed; 
TÜSİAD is composed of direct members representing companies and leads a platform founded by sectoral and regional business federations (TÜRKONFED: Turkish Confederation of Enterprise and Business);
TÜSİAD is a window of business through its representations in Brussels, Berlin, Paris London, Washington DC.
TÜSİAD is and committed to monitor and promote Turkey’s economic competitiveness, institutional reform process and membership to the European Union.

communication_activities:
Our communication activities related to the above EU policies are limited to technical and informational outreach rather than public advocacy campaigns. They include: 
- presentations and panel discussions at wine and agrifood industry events on the practical impact of EU rules on AI, data use and online sales for small wineries, retailers and HoReCa operators; 
- articles, blog posts and newsletters explaining in accessible language how EU consumer protection, data protection and food information rules apply in digital wine services;
- sharing aggregated, anonymised insights with policy-relevant stakeholders in the context of consultations or expert meetings. 
These activities are non-partisan, evidence-based and focused on helping market actors comply with EU legislation and use trustworthy AI and data practices. 
We do not conduct political advertising or grassroots mobilisation, do not offer gifts or hospitality, and adhere to the Transparency Register Code of Conduct, meeting-disclosure and data-protection rules.

