We follow a series of legislative and non-legislative initiatives at the intersection of EU trade, climate, industrial policy, and the circular economy. These include: 
- The EU Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism, focusing on the legislative package announced on 17 December, including a legislative proposal for amending Regulation (EU) 2023/956 as regards the extension of its scope to downstream goods and anti-circumvention measures, and implementing/delegated acts;
- The Eco-design for Sustainable Products Regulation (ESPR), with a focus on delegated acts with product-specific requirements for iron and steel (expected for 2026) and textiles and apparel (expected for 2027);
- Communication from the Commission on a European Steel and Metals Action Plan and related legislative initiatives, including the forthcoming legislative proposal for an Industrial Accelerator Act.
- The upcoming Circular Economy Act; 
- The implementation of the EU-South Africa Clean Trade and Investment Partnership; 
- Following the negotiations and implementation of EU Free Trade Agreements, with a focus on ongoing negotiations with India.

Communication from the Commission on the Clean Industrial Deal;

Communication from the Commission on an EU Industrial Strategy;

Proposal for a Regulation establishing a framework of measures for strengthening Europe’s net-zero technology manufacturing ecosystem (Net-Zero Industry Act);

In this context, interest representation activities may also relate to initiatives concerning European industrial competitiveness and supply chain resilience, as well as relevant EU legislative frameworks in the fields of energy, climate and strategic infrastructure where these are directly connected to the above-mentioned initiatives.

