Our association engages in EU policy engagement activities primarily through the expertise and in-kind contributions of its member organisations at the moment. We consolidate practical feedback from our members (SMEs, innovation actors and digital ecosystem stakeholders) and, where relevant, our representatives participate in public consultations, stakeholder events and expert discussions, with the aim of supporting evidence-based policy design and implementation in the fields of digitalisation and innovation.

In particular, our engagement relates to the following EU legislative and policy frameworks/initiatives:

Horizon Europe - EU Framework Programme for Research and Innovation;

Digital Europe Programme - supporting strategic digital transformation initiatives;

AI Act - EU regulation on artificial intelligence (compliance, ethics and deployment aspects);

AI Factories / AI Sandboxes - EU-level initiatives promoting AI experimentation, innovation and testing environments;

European Digital Innovation Hubs (EDIHs) - policies and initiatives supporting SMEs and public sector organisations in the uptake of digital technologies and access to knowledge, testing facilities and finance.

Through these activities, we contribute structured, practice-based input from our member community to support the effective development and uptake of EU instruments, aligned with the needs of innovation ecosystems and digital transformation priorities.

Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and of the Council laying down harmonised rules on artificial intelligence (Artificial Intelligence Act), including delegated and implementing acts under development;

Communication from the Commission on AI Continent Action Plan (COM(2025) 97), including the AI Gigafactories initiative and associated procurement frameworks;

Regulation (EU) 2023/1781 of the European Parliament and of the Council establishing a framework of measures for strengthening Europe's semiconductor ecosystem (European Chips Act);

Horizon Europe — Work Programme 2025–2027, Cluster 4 (Digital, Industry and Space) and Cluster 1 (Health);

Communication from the Commission on the European Industrial Strategy and updates thereto concerning advanced computing and AI infrastructure.

