goals:
The association's charitable goal is to improve equestrian education and qualifications worldwide, with the ultimate goal of promoting the welfare of the horse (and rider).
It pursues this goal by:
- developing, promoting and maintaining international standards for equestrian qualifications;
- promoting horsemanship, knowledge, skills, safety and welfare in equestrian sports;
- facilitating international exchange and recognition of qualifications;
- supporting members and partners in developing and implementing national training systems, with a focus on inclusive, well-being-oriented standards;
- organizing training courses, seminars, conferences and other initiatives to promote these objectives.
The association operates on a global scale, on a non-profit basis and in accordance with the principles of transparency, inclusion and horse welfare.

