goals:
Fundacja EdukWings is a Polish non-profit foundation based in Katowice, established to promote social inclusion, education and international exchange. 
Our goals are: 
(1) social assistance for marginalised groups at risk of exclusion; 
(2) educational projects and international exchanges; 
(3) promoting education and socio-economic development through digital transformation and innovation; 
(4) environmental protection and sustainable development; 
(5) social, educational and vocational activation of people with disabilities and senior citizens. 

We operate through training, workshops, language education, school exchanges, digital innovation projects and capacity-building for civil society organisations.

eu_legislative_proposals:
Fundacja EdukWings monitors and engages with EU policies in the following areas: 
(1) Erasmus+ Programme (KA1 and KA2) for international mobility and educational exchange projects targeting youth, adults and people with disabilities; 
(2) European Social Fund Plus (ESF+) for social inclusion, employment activation and anti-discrimination initiatives; 
(3) EU Strategy for the Rights of Persons with Disabilities 2021-2030; 
(4) European Skills Agenda for upskilling, digital literacy and vocational activation; 
(5) EU Action Plan on Integration and Inclusion 2021-2027; 
(6) EU Green Deal and related education and awareness programmes on environmental sustainability. 
The foundation seeks to align its project portfolio with these frameworks to access EU co-financing and contribute to their implementation at the local and national level in Poland.

communication_activities:
Fundacja EdukWings conducts the following communication activities related to the EU policies above: 
(1) Social media outreach via LinkedIn and other platforms raising awareness of EU-funded opportunities for marginalised communities in the Katowice/Silesia region; 
(2) Organisation of community integration events, language cafés and workshops accessible to people with disabilities, seniors and migrants; 
(3) Collaboration with local NGO support centre COP Katowice to disseminate information about EU programmes to other civil society organisations; 
(4) Publication of educational materials and guides on digital skills, language learning and social inclusion in both Polish and English; 
(5) Participation in NGO capacity-building events to support other organisations in accessing EU funding.

