My targeted activities within the European context include legal review, advisory services, policy proposals, as well as the organization of events, conferences, and publications in relation to key European procedures and regulatory frameworks. In particular, my work focuses on the following areas:
- Renewable Energy Directive – assessment of its scope and development of proposals aimed at supporting regulatory evolution in the energy transition sector, including alignment with EU decarbonisation targets;
- EU public procurement framework (Directives 2014/23/EU, 2014/24/EU, 2014/25/EU) – organization of conferences, training sessions, and operational activities to support compliance with European rules, particularly following the implementation of Legislative Decree No. 36/2023 in Italy, with increasing focus on sustainability criteria and lifecycle-based procurement models;
- Green Public Procurement (GPP) – analysis and promotion of recent European initiatives aimed at integrating environmental and climate criteria into public procurement procedures, including the development of proposals to strengthen mandatory sustainability requirements and ESG-based evaluation frameworks;
- Digital Markets Act – analysis of its impact on competition in digital markets, including assessments aimed at contributing to fair and open market conditions;
- European Artificial Intelligence Act – evaluation of legal and regulatory implications of technological developments, drafting of publications, and contribution to the debate through events and conferences;
- Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive (CSRD – Directive (EU) 2022/2464) – advanced assistance to clients in adapting governance, risk management, and reporting systems to the new European Sustainability Reporting Standards (ESRS), including double materiality assessments, value chain analysis, and integration of Climate Transition Plans in line with EU climate neutrality objectives and related obligations under evolving EU frameworks (including links with the Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence Directive – CSDDD);
- Climate Transition Plans and ESG governance – legal support in the design, implementation, and disclosure of transition strategies aligned with EU climate targets, including decarbonisation pathways, emissions reduction targets, and consistency with regulatory expectations under CSRD and forthcoming due diligence obligations;

