eu_legislative_proposals:
Swity d.o.o. follows and aligns its activities with key European Union policies related to sustainable food production, environmental protection, energy efficiency and circular economy.

The company particularly follows:

• European Green Deal – reduction of CO₂ emissions, renewable energy, energy efficiency and sustainable waste management;

• Farm to Fork Strategy – food safety, sustainable food processing and resilient supply chains;

• EU industrial and SME policies – modernization, digitalization and competitiveness of the food industry sector;

• Circular Economy Action Plan – bio-waste utilization and environmentally responsible wastewater management;

• Cohesion Policy, InvestEU and WBIF initiatives – development of investment projects related to food processing, environmental protection and rural development;

• EU enlargement and alignment policies for the Western Balkans – compliance with EU food safety, hygiene and environmental standards.

Swity also follows EU legislation related to food labeling, packaging materials, greenhouse gas emissions, water management and waste treatment.

communication_activities:
Swity d.o.o. carries out communication activities aimed at promoting sustainable development, local agriculture, food safety and environmentally responsible food production in line with European Union policies.

Activities include:
• participation in regional and international trade fairs and business events related to the food industry and sustainable development;
• organization of presentations and visits for partners, local producers, schools and local community representatives;
• publication of promotional and educational content through the company website and social media channels;
• workshops and internal trainings related to HACCP standards, energy efficiency, sustainable packaging and environmental protection;
• preparation of investment and development projects related to EU policies such as the European Green Deal, Farm to Fork Strategy, circular economy and digital transition;
• communication with partners, institutions and organizations regarding financing opportunities through EU and international programs.

The company also implements local community support and educational initiatives promoting sustainable food production. Future activities include projects related to renewable energy, wastewater treatment, energy efficiency and development of new production capacities.

