goals:
PEMA's purpose is to serve the following non-profit interests of international utility in the sector of port and heavy industrial handling equipments:
- to provide a forum for discussion and collective action, study, research and debate on economic, social or public issues of general interest;
- to promote and achieve the establishment of international standards or regulations relating to product safety and performance;
- to participate in all dialogues with and to represent its Members vis-à-vis all public or private, international, EU or national organizations dealing, directly or indirectly, with problems or issues relating to the Industry;
- to collect and disseminate statistical information relating to the Industry in a manner and to the extent permitted by law, and within the limitations provided in the present Bylaws;
- to achieve all that is useful with regard to the accomplishment of any of the above objectives without pecuniary profit to PEMA or any Member.

eu_legislative_proposals:
MRIGlobal’s engagement with European Union institutions focuses on policy areas related to chemical, biological, radiological and nuclear (CBRN) preparedness and response, public health emergency readiness, and civil protection coordination.

In particular, MRIGlobal’s activities relate to:

(1) The European Union framework for CBRN risk mitigation and capacity building, including initiatives under the CBRN Centres of Excellence;

(2) European Union policies and programmes on health emergency preparedness and response, including activities led by the Directorate-General for Health Emergency Preparedness and Response (HERA);

(3) European Union civil protection and disaster risk management policies, including the Union Civil Protection Mechanism;

(4) European Union research and innovation programmes supporting security, resilience, and biodefence capabilities.

MRIGlobal’s objective is to contribute technical expertise and participate in collaborative programmes that strengthen global and European preparedness for biological and other cross-border threats.

