communication_activities:
Inventec Performance Chemicals may contribute to public consultations, stakeholder consultations, workshops, technical exchanges and industry discussions related to European industrial policy, strategic value chains and sustainability objectives.

Such activities may concern, among others:

- the implementation and future evolution of the European Chips Act and related initiatives aimed at strengthening Europe's semiconductor ecosystem and technological sovereignty;

- the activities of the European Semiconductor Alliance and its working groups;

- the activities of the Critical Chemicals Alliance related to critical molecules, industrial resilience, supply chain security and strategic production capacities;

- discussions regarding the transition towards more sustainable industrial solutions, including the development of lower-impact alternatives to substances subject to increasing regulatory scrutiny;

- industrial competitiveness, innovation, advanced manufacturing and supply chain resilience within the European Economic Area.

Inventec may provide technical expertise, industrial feedback, market insights and information derived from its manufacturing, R&D and application activities in Europe. Such contributions may take the form of responses to public consultations, position papers, technical exchanges, workshops, conferences, industry events or collaborative projects involving industrial stakeholders, public institutions and research organisations.

Inventec has a long-standing commitment to supporting the development of sustainable industrial solutions. This includes previous contributions by company representatives to international discussions on climate-related technologies and environmental transition pathways, as well as ongoing efforts to develop innovative materials with reduced environmental impact for strategic industries such as semiconductors, electronics and advanced manufacturing.

organisation_members:
Inventec Performance Chemicals participates in and contributes to a number of industrial, technical and professional networks related to electronics, semiconductors, advanced manufacturing and specialty chemicals.

These include, among others:

• GIFAS (Groupement des Industries Françaises Aéronautiques et Spatiales), through participation in industry exchanges and working groups relevant to aerospace, defence and strategic technologies;

• SMTA (Surface Mount Technology Association), supporting technical exchanges and industry developments in electronics assembly and manufacturing;

• SEMI and semiconductor-related industry initiatives and events, contributing to discussions on semiconductor manufacturing, materials and supply chains;

• French electronics industry organisations and networks, including participation in activities supporting the development of the electronics ecosystem in France and Europe;

* Major European industry events such as the Productronica (Germany) or SLAM Conference in France. Although they may not be directly funded by the EU, they aim to support and strengthen European resilience.

• Industry consultations and exchanges related to chemical regulations and industrial competitiveness, including topics relevant to REACH or the the Chips Act for example.

* Inventec is also seeking active participation in the European Semiconductor Alliance and its working groups, with the objective of contributing industrial expertise on the supply chain resilience, sustainability challenges and innovation opportunities supporting Europe's technological sovereignty.

* We are also seeking to get involved in the COP and various carbon markets, as our solutions enable our clients to significantly reduce their CO₂ emissions;

Inventec also collaborates regularly with public institutions, research organisations, industrial partners and regional innovation ecosystems in support of European industrial competitiveness and technological sovereignty.

