Regulation (EU) 2024/1787 on the reduction of methane emissions in the energy sector (the "EU Methane Regulation"), in particular its implementation through delegated and implementing acts. Specific areas of interest include:

Leak detection and repair (LDAR) requirements;
Measurement, reporting and verification (MRV), including the equivalence of monitoring and reporting obligations for energy imports;
The methane intensity methodology and standards applying to importers of fossil energy.

This sits within the broader context of EU energy and climate policy under the European Green Deal and the EU's contribution to the Global Methane Pledge.

