Main EU legislative proposals or policies targeted:
EU Money Monitor's only activity that may fall within the scope of the Register is advocacy for greater transparency and public verifiability of EU public funding. It pursues no outcome for any client, member or commercial interest, and no outcome other than improved public access to EU funding data. Files followed and engaged:
•	the revision of Regulation (EC, Euratom) No 883/2013 (the OLAF Regulation), including the public consultation on its revision;
•	the EU Financial Transparency System and the planned "Single Gateway" integrating funding data across all management modes under the 2028–2034 Multiannual Financial Framework;
•	the follow-up to European Court of Auditors Special Report 11/2025, "Transparency of EU funding granted to NGOs";
•	the European Commission's anti-fraud strategy following European Court of Auditors Special Report 18/2026;
•	the legal definition of "NGO" and beneficiary-level transparency in EU funding, including recipient identification, classification and final-beneficiary disclosure.

communication_activities:
Our organisation engages in communication activities related to the above-mentioned EU initiatives primarily through participation in industry associations, stakeholder platforms and public events.

These activities include:
- contributing to exchanges and meetings organised by the European Commission services and European Parliament members, either directly or through industry associations and coalitions;
- participating in conferences, workshops and stakeholder dialogues addressing sustainable materials, packaging and the bioeconomy;
- providing technical input and sharing expertise in the context of public consultations and informal exchanges with EU stakeholders;
- engaging with relevant value chain actors to contribute to discussions on the development and implementation of EU policies affecting bio-based and biodegradable materials.

Interactions are generally of a technical and informative nature and aim at supporting evidence-based policymaking.

