eu_legislative_proposals:
EUFASA is primarily an advocacy and policy organization, not a lobbying body focused on specific EU legislative files. Most of its work targets national Ministries of Foreign Affairs (MFAs) and the European External Action Service rather than seeking amendments to major EU legislation.
Although EUFASA has not been a prominent public campaigner on these legislative files, its recommendations are closely aligned with:
European Pillar of Social Rights (social protection, equal opportunities, work-life balance);
EU Social Security Coordination Regulations (cross-border social security rights);
Directive (EU) 2019/1158 (family support and work-life balance);
EU policies on professional qualification recognition and labour mobility, which can affect spouses accompanying diplomats abroad.

communication_activities:
EUFASA mainly:
publishes research and policy papers;
issues recommendations to European MFAs and the EEAS;
advocates improvements in administrative policies affecting diplomatic families;
encourages reforms that are compatible with broader EU social and employment policies.

We are active in:

* Organising youth exchanges;
* Participating in pilot projects related to national civic service schemes;
* Organising events and awareness campaigns on solidarity, culture and environmental issues;
* Implementing projects supported by the European Parliament, such as BuildEU2.
* Participating in two IMREG INFOME projects, specifically targeting the communication about EU Funding, with one being a project that we specifically coordinate

