goals:
Young Early Starters NV (YES) is a Belgian fintech start-up developing a real-stock investment platform for children aged 8 to 18, combining genuine equity ownership with structured financial education and mandatory parental approval on every transaction.
YES seeks engagement with EU institutions to monitor and contribute to policy developments directly relevant to its activities, in particular:

the application of MiFID II to investment services involving minors;
the implementation of ESMA guidelines on gamification in financial services;
GDPR requirements for the processing of children's personal data (Article 8);
emerging initiatives on financial literacy under the Retail Investment Strategy.

YES aims to engage constructively with policymakers to support a regulatory framework that enables responsible financial education for young people while ensuring appropriate consumer protection standards.

communication_activities:
Some recent examples:

We wrote several Open Letters to the President of the Commission  and several Commissioners:
- Call for an EU-wide mechanism on windfall profits by the fossil fuel industry - April 2026;
- Our opinion on the new European Arctic Policy - March 2026;
- Concern Regarding the Reversal of the Combustion Engine Phase-Out - February 2026;
- European Grandparents for Climate call on the European Commission to refrain from harmful Omnibus processes - December 2025.

We demonstrated:
- We stood in front of Alden Biesen where European leaders met, demanding not to weaken the Green Deal - February 2026;
- On 31st of May 2024 our members blew a whistle in front of national parliaments as Wake Up call for the 2024 European Elections.

Our members were present:
- At COP 30 and delivered a Letter to EU leaders;
- At the First Conference on Transitioning away from Fossil Fuels in Santa Marta, Colombia with a Statement of EGC.

Details can be found in News items on our website: https://grandparentsforclimate.eu/.

