GeoCodis follows EU policies, programmes and initiatives related to the practical use of Earth Observation, geospatial data, artificial intelligence, digital platforms and environmental information systems in support of public policies, operational services and international cooperation.

The most relevant EU policy areas for GeoCodis include the EU Space Programme, Copernicus, Destination Earth, Horizon Europe, Digital Europe, climate adaptation, water resilience, disaster risk reduction, environmental monitoring, biodiversity and wetlands, sustainable infrastructure, public-sector digital transformation, development cooperation and EU external action.

GeoCodis is particularly interested in EU initiatives that promote the use of satellite data, geospatial analytics, artificial intelligence, digital twins, cloud-based processing, early warning systems and decision-support platforms for climate resilience, water management, flood and drought monitoring, infrastructure risk assessment, land-use monitoring, biodiversity protection and environmental reporting.

Relevant EU policies and initiatives include, but are not limited to:

EU Space Programme and Copernicus, including the use of Sentinel satellite data, Copernicus services, Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem and downstream Earth Observation applications;

Destination Earth, including digital twins, climate and weather extremes, data-driven modelling, simulation, forecasting and decision-support services;

Horizon Europe, especially clusters and missions related to climate, energy, mobility, civil security, digital technologies, food, bioeconomy, natural resources, agriculture and environment;

Digital Europe Programme, including artificial intelligence, data spaces, cloud-to-edge infrastructure, high-performance computing, digital public services and digital transformation of public administrations;

EU Mission on Adaptation to Climate Change, including support to regions, cities and communities in improving climate resilience, risk assessment, adaptation planning and deployment of climate services;

EU climate adaptation and resilience policies, including climate risk management, disaster preparedness, flood and drought risk reduction, early warning systems and resilience of critical infrastructure;

EU water-related policies, including water resilience, water resources management, river basin management, flood risk management, drought monitoring, water quality monitoring and digital support tools for water utilities and public authorities;

EU environmental policies related to biodiversity, wetlands, land degradation, ecosystem monitoring, nature restoration, pollution monitoring, environmental reporting and evidence-based environmental governance;

EU civil protection, disaster risk reduction and security-related policies where geospatial intelligence, Earth Observation, situational awareness and infrastructure risk assessment can support preparedness, response and recovery;

EU international cooperation and development policies, including Global Gateway, Team Europe Initiatives and external action programmes that support water security, climate adaptation, sustainable infrastructure, digital transformation and capacity building in partner countries.

GeoCodis represents its own professional and business interests and seeks to contribute technical expertise, implementation experience and project references to EU discussions, partnerships, funding programmes and implementation mechanisms where Earth Observation, GIS, artificial intelligence and digital decision-support systems can support better policy implementation and operational outcomes.

goals:
