Communication activities
ARIS representatives will participate in meetings with representatives of the European Commission, the European Parliament and the European External Action Service (EEAS) in Brussels on and around 13 July 2026, in connection with the ARIS Board Meeting and diplomatic dinner.
The purpose of these meetings is to present the work of the Alliance of Rabbis in Islamic States (ARIS) and to exchange views on:
freedom of religion or belief;
protection of Jewish communities and religious heritage in Muslim-majority countries;
combating antisemitism;
interfaith dialogue;
EU engagement with religious communities in the Middle East, North Africa, Central Asia and Sub-Saharan Africa.
The meetings will consist of policy discussions and exchanges of expertise based on ARIS's experience supporting Jewish communities throughout the Muslim world.

