Custorian's work concerns the EU framework on child digital safety and child protection, in particular:
• the EU Action Plan on the protection of children against crime (DG HOME);
• the proposed Regulation to prevent and combat child sexual abuse (COM(2022) 209) and the recast Child Sexual Abuse Directive;
• the Digital Services Act (Regulation (EU) 2022/2065), especially Article 28 (protection of minors);
• the AI Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689);
• eIDAS 2.0 (Regulation (EU) 2024/1183), on age assurance via the European Digital Identity Wallet;
• the GDPR (Regulation (EU) 2016/679), Article 8;
• the EU Strategy on the Rights of the Child and the Better Internet for Kids (BIK+) strategy;
• the President's Special Panel on child safety online.
