FNOPI intende contribuire e influenzare le seguenti politiche, atti legislativi e iniziative dell’Unione europea:
Regolamento sullo Spazio Europeo dei Dati Sanitari (European Health Data Space – EHDS), relativo all’accesso, condivisione e utilizzo dei dati sanitari elettronici;
Direttiva 2005/36/CE sul riconoscimento delle qualifiche professionali, come modificata dalla Direttiva 2013/55/UE, con riferimento alla professione infermieristica;
Regolamento (UE) 2021/522 – Programma EU4Health (2021–2027), per il rafforzamento dei sistemi sanitari e della forza lavoro sanitaria;
Decisione (UE) 2022/2371 sulle gravi minacce per la salute a carattere transfrontaliero, nell’ambito dell’Unione europea della salute;
Regolamento (UE) 2022/2370 che rafforza il ruolo del Centro europeo per la prevenzione e il controllo delle malattie (ECDC);
Regolamento (UE) 2022/123 relativo al rafforzamento del ruolo dell’Agenzia europea per i medicinali (EMA) nelle crisi sanitarie;
Comunicazione della Commissione sulla carenza di personale sanitario nell’UE e iniziative collegate alla Health Workforce, incluse le azioni sulla pianificazione e sostenibilità della forza lavoro;
Strategia europea per la sanità digitale (eHealth / Digital Health), comprese le iniziative su telemedicina e interoperabilità (es. MyHealth@EU);
Pilastro europeo dei diritti sociali – Principio 16 (assistenza sanitaria) e le iniziative collegate all’accesso alle cure e alla qualità dell’assistenza;
Programmi e politiche su invecchiamento attivo e cronicità (es. iniziative nell’ambito della Silver Economy e EU4Health);
Quadri europei sulle competenze professionali (es. European Skills Agenda) con impatto sulla formazione e sull’aggiornamento degli infermieri.

Our organization monitors EU policy developments and legislative proposals affecting business competitiveness, digital transformation, and regulatory simplification. We focus on areas relevant to SMEs and businesses operating across European markets.

Key areas of interest include:

- Competitiveness and Single Market integration, including the "One Europe, One Market" roadmap and initiatives to remove barriers to the four freedoms;
- Simplification of EU rules and reduction of administrative burdens for businesses, including the target to reduce administrative burden by at least 25% for all businesses;
- Digital economy and AI regulation, including implementation of the AI Act and related transparency obligations;
- Digital sovereignty initiatives, including semiconductor strategy, cloud infrastructure, and data policy;
- Industrial policy and sector-specific competitiveness measures affecting manufacturing, automotive, and clean energy sectors;
- Corporate sustainability, ESG reporting, and responsible business conduct;
- SME support measures, including incentives for business growth and scaling up;
- Energy security and transition policies, including diversification of energy sources;
- Crisis resilience and disaster management, including civil protection mechanisms;
- Education, skills development, and workforce training for competitive Europe.

We follow legislative work of the European Parliament, Council, and Commission, with particular attention to proposals under the 2026 Commission Work Programme, including omnibus simplification packages and sector-specific initiatives. Our interest covers both ongoing legislative procedures and emerging policy frameworks that may impact business environment and investment climate in the EU.

goals:
De vennootschap heeft tot voorwerp – zowel in België als in het buitenland – de krachten te bundelen voor :
- de bevordering, ondersteuning, en uitvoering van innovatieve ontwikkelingen en/of projecten, van welke aard ook, in de visserij, vissector of aanverwante sectoren;
- initiatie, ondersteuning en uitvoering van projecten die bijdragen tot een duurzamere visserij of vissector, een efficiënte betrouwbare dienstverlening naar de aanvoerders en de kopers, een breed en kwaliteitsvol visaanbod;
- de commercialisatie en de exploitatie van visveilingen; de verhandeling, de verkoop, de opslag, de bewaring, de distributie, de kwaliteitsborging en de bewerking van vis en aanverwante producten;
- de bevordering van de samenwerking tussen alle marktactoren.

