eu_legislative_proposals:
The activities of the Polish Sugar Producers Association (Związek Producentów Cukru w Polsce – ZPC) at EU level concern, in particular, the following EU policies, legislative proposals and regulatory areas:

Common Agricultural Policy (CAP), including the future legal framework of the CAP and provisions relevant to the sugar sector;
Common Market Organisation (CMO) for agricultural products – Regulation (EU) No 1308/2013, including provisions concerning the sugar sector and contractual relations between sugar beet growers and sugar producers, in particular Article 125 and Annex X;
EU trade policy and market access for sugar, including the EU–Ukraine Association Agreement / Deep and Comprehensive Free Trade Area (DCFTA) and its provisions concerning agricultural products and sugar;
EU–Mercosur trade relations, including the EU–Mercosur agreement and the treatment of sugar and sugar-containing products;
EU legislation on packaging and packaging waste, in particular Regulation (EU) 2025/40 on packaging and packaging waste (PPWR), including provisions concerning PFAS in food-contact packaging;
EU rules on food additives and sweeteners, including Regulation (EC) No 1333/2008 on food additives;
EU regulatory framework for new genomic techniques (NGTs) and their application in agriculture;
EU legislation concerning soil monitoring and soil resilience, including the proposed Soil Monitoring Law;
EU climate and carbon-border policies, including the Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism (CBAM) and its implications for the sugar sector;
EU food labelling and consumer information policies, including the ongoing and forthcoming development/revision of EU rules concerning food information to consumers and nutrition-related information;
EU food and feed safety legislation, including the Commission's Food and Feed Safety Omnibus initiatives;
EU policies concerning water resilience and adaptation to water scarcity, including the future European strategy for water resilience.

The Foundation's EU-level engagement consists of awareness-raising and public dialogue; it does not advocate on specific legislative files or propose amendments. Its event at the European Parliament on 15 October 2026, "Inner Peace, Outer Engagement", addresses the link between inner well-being and care for the environment and relates to the following EU policy frameworks:

– Communication from the Commission on a comprehensive approach to mental health (COM(2023) 298, 7 June 2023);
– European Parliament resolution of 12 December 2023 on mental health;
– 8th Environment Action Programme to 2030 (Decision (EU) 2022/591).

The Foundation has not produced or commissioned any position papers, surveys or advocacy campaigns and has no current plans to do so.

