ANcybernetics’ activities in relation to EU institutions concern policies supporting the sustainable, innovative and secure use of the marine environment, the development and deployment of advanced ocean technologies, and the competitiveness of the European blue economy.

In particular, the organisation follows and may contribute to discussions concerning:
• the European Ocean Pact (COM(2025)281) and its implementation, including the forthcoming European Ocean Act, EU ocean governance, maritime spatial planning and policies supporting ocean research, innovation and technological development;
• OceanEye – the EU Ocean Observation Initiative (COM(2026)268), including the development of European ocean observation capabilities, autonomous marine data collection, marine monitoring technologies, interoperability and availability of ocean data, and the European Digital Twin of the Ocean;
• the EU Mission “Restore our Ocean and Waters by 2030” and related Horizon Europe research and innovation policies, particularly in relation to marine ecosystem and habitat monitoring, biodiversity assessment, environmental restoration, pollution prevention and the deployment and scaling-up of innovative ocean technologies;
• EU sustainable blue economy policies and initiatives aimed at strengthening the competitiveness, technological sovereignty and innovation capacity of European maritime industries, including support for SMEs, start-ups and emerging ocean-technology sectors;
• EU marine environmental policy, including the Marine Strategy Framework Directive, the Nature Restoration Regulation and related initiatives concerning the monitoring, protection and restoration of marine and coastal ecosystems;
• EU policies concerning the security, resilience, monitoring and inspection of critical underwater and seabed infrastructure, including submarine communication and energy cables and the implementation of the EU Action Plan on Cable Security;
• EU maritime security, defence and dual-use innovation policies where relevant to autonomous underwater systems, maritime situational awareness, ocean monitoring and protection of critical seabed infrastructure;
• EU research, innovation and industrial policies supporting autonomous systems, artificial intelligence, robotics, marine sensing technologies and the transfer of research results towards industrial and commercial applications.

ANcybernetics’ engagement is primarily aimed at contributing technical and industrial expertise from the European underwater robotics and ocean-technology sector and at supporting dialogue between innovative SMEs, research organisations, maritime stakeholders and EU institutions.

