communication_activities:
1. Participation in meetings or civil society consultations with different EU representatives and bodies to share information concerning the state of human rights in Egypt, particularly in relation to security policy, asylum and migration, socioeconomic rights, macro-financial assistance, and arms trade. Between June 2023 and July 2026, we have participated in over 30 meetings/consultations with the following representatives or stakeholders:
- MEPs, including Mounir Satouri, Tineke Strik, and other members of the DROI, AFET, and DEVE Committees;
Desk officers from DG MENA, DG HOME, the EU Commission Directorate-General for the Middle East, North Africa and the Gulf, the EUAA, and the EEAS;
- EU Special Rapporteur for Human Rights;
- EU Delegation to Egypt (EEAS)
- COARM working group within the EU Council, in the context of annual consultations with civil society (COARM-NGOs Forum)
2. Participation in a public event at the EU Parliament to present research findings on human rights issues, on 28th June 2023, titled “Italian and EU Arms Fueling Repression in Egypt” (https://europeecologie.eu/italian-and-eu-arms-in-egypt)
3. Submission of input, in the form of research briefs and joint civil society statements, presented to MEPs and competent offices within the EU Commission (https://aeur.eu/f/j2v)

