SALUS Alliance focuses on EU policies and initiatives concerning public health, prevention of non-communicable diseases, health promotion, cancer prevention, cardiovascular and metabolic disease prevention, tobacco and nicotine regulation, alcohol-related harm, obesity prevention, nutrition, physical activity, addiction prevention, mental health, health inequalities and evidence-based harm reduction.
Relevant EU Agenda:
•	Europe’s Beating Cancer Plan;
•	EU Safe Hearts Plan
•	EU initiatives on non-communicable diseases;
•	EU tobacco control and nicotine regulation, including policies related to the Tobacco Products Directive and related regulatory initiatives;
•	EU policies on alcohol-related harm;
•	EU initiatives on obesity, nutrition and physical activity;
•	EU initiatives on cardiovascular and metabolic disease prevention;
•	EU public health policies addressing addiction prevention, mental health, health inequalities and behavioural risk factors.

A3M follows and contributes to EU policies and legislative initiatives affecting the mining, minerals and metals industries, in particular:
EU industrial policy and competitiveness, including the Clean Industrial Deal and the Industrial Accelerator Act;
the Critical Raw Materials Act and EU policies on security and diversification of raw material supply chains;
EU climate policy, including the EU Emissions Trading System (EU ETS) and the Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism (CBAM);
EU trade policy, trade defence instruments and measures addressing global overcapacity and non-market practices;
EU energy policy and measures affecting energy-intensive industries and electricity costs;
circular economy and recycling policies, including scrap and secondary raw materials;
environmental legislation applicable to mining and metallurgical activities, including water, industrial emissions, waste and permitting;
EU sustainable finance, State aid and financing instruments supporting industrial investment and strategic capacities;
EU research, innovation and skills policies relevant to the mining, minerals and metals value chains.

JustBrussels follows and contributes research-based input to the following EU policies and initiatives:

- ProtectEU – European Internal Security Strategy, in particular community policing, crime prevention and cross-border police cooperation;
- EU policy on the prevention of radicalisation and violent extremism, including the work of the EU Knowledge Hub on Prevention of Radicalisation;
- Pact on Migration and Asylum and its implementation, from the perspective of rights-based governance and public security;
- EU Action Plan on Integration and Inclusion 2021–2027;
- EU Strategy on Victims' Rights and EU initiatives on access to justice, legal aid and alternative dispute resolution;
- EU Anti-Money Laundering package and the Anti-Money Laundering Authority (AMLA), as regards financial transparency in the non-profit sector;
- EU funding programmes relevant to our field: CERV, Justice Programme, Internal Security Fund and Horizon Europe Cluster 3 (Civil Security for Society).

communication_activities:
JustBrussels communicates on the EU policies above through its trilingual website (EN/FR/NL), www.justbrussels.org, which presents its research areas in the fields of justice, security and society; studies and publications will be added as projects develop.

Planned activities:
- seminars and training sessions for practitioners, civil society and young people on security, justice and social cohesion;
- a newsletter informing subscribers about our activities and relevant EU policy developments;
- publication of research notes and policy recommendations;
- participation in European Commission public consultations;
- partnership in EU-funded projects (CERV, Justice Programme, Internal Security Fund, Horizon Europe).

eu_legislative_proposals:
DiGas (Latvia) develops hydrogen and biomethane internal-combustion retrofits for diesel locomotives and seeks to inform EU external cooperation policy on rail decarbonisation in partner countries. Specific instruments addressed:
– Regulation (EU) 2021/947 establishing the Neighbourhood, Development and International Cooperation Instrument – Global Europe (NDICI-Global Europe), in particular its programming for transport and energy-transition cooperation;
– Global Gateway strategy (JOIN(2021) 30 final), sustainable transport and clean-hydrogen pillars;
– EU–Viet Nam Just Energy Transition Partnership (JETP) and the Multiannual Indicative Programme for Viet Nam 2021–2027.

Upcoming meeting: 19 November 2026, 11:00–12:30, European Commission, DG International Partnerships (DG INTPA), building L-41, Brussels. Subject: “Presentation of Latvian company DiGas with Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Latvia” — presentation of DiGas’s hydrogen locomotive retrofit technology and its relevance to Global Gateway rail decarbonisation in partner countries (Viet Nam). DiGas role: presenter, together with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Latvia.

