communication_activities:
ITA operates worldwide through a large network of Trade Agencies Offices linked to Italian Embassies and Consulates and works closely with local authorities and businesses, providing information, support and advice to Italian companies, by facilitating their access to the European Union’s funding programmes. 
The  main goal is to help Italian SMEs seize opportunities for growth and development at an European and international level, by assisting them in identifying suitable EU funding and tender opportunities. To this purpose, ITA makes available user-friendly information and knowledge on the decision-making processes of the EU and the European Investment Bank (EIB) in order to establish a direct line between the Italian SMEs and trade associations and these institutions. 

The main activities carried out are:

Organization of information events:
- Informative seminars / Webinars in Italy and abroad dedicated to EU programmes, with a focus on countries and/or sectors, in collaboration with the EU institutions;
- Training seminars / Webinars on EU project management methodologies in collaboration with experts;
- Missions of entrepreneurs to the EU Commission, in Brussels, aimed at facilitating direct contact between SMEs and the DGs responsible for geographic or thematic funding programs;
- Information, assistance and networking actions and guidance on EU Calls for Proposals and Calls for tenders;
- Elaboration of deliverables (brochures, manuals, guides, etc.) in Italian language, to facilitate the awareness of SMEs of EU programmes and project management methodologies 
- Publication in the Agency website of a monthly newsletter "Opportunità dall'Europa", an information tool on EU funding, policy-making, events and news.

